<GuidePage
  title="Turn a Pattern Cut List into One Fabric Plan"
  description="Compile an external pattern's rectangular cuts by fabric without recreating the quilt design."
  eyebrow="Common Workflow"
  guideSlug="turn-pattern-cut-list-into-plan"
  guideCategory="workflow"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Start from the pattern's cutting table</h2><p>
      Create each named fabric, then enter or paste one row per repeated
      rectangular cut. Preserve the pattern's Cut/Finished wording and any
      direction or WOF-strip constraint.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Add comparison data separately</h2><p>
      If the pattern states yardage, enter Pattern says and its usable WOF when
      known. This external reference never replaces the cut list and never
      becomes the stock-aware shortfall.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Calculate one joint plan per fabric</h2><p>
      QuiltClarity considers different piece groups together so compatible cuts
      can share row width. Review the shopping amount, then cut from the
      selected placements and instructions.
    </p>
  </section>
  <p>
    <a href="/guides/enter-a-cut-list/">Learn the fast cut-list entry paths</a>.
  </p>
</GuidePage>
